  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.7</data>
  <data key="d36">An increase in the risk of interference raises market risk premia and prompts traders and buyers to hedge or stockpile crude, driving spot and near-term futures prices higher even before physical flows are curtailed.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">us_iran_conflict</data>
