<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::kinetic_attack_intensity" target="global_energy_reorder::supply_disruption_level" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.85</data>
  <data key="d36">Increased kinetic strikes on ports, pipelines, refineries and tankers causes direct physical damage and port closures, interrupting transport and processing nodes and raising measured supply-chain disruption.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d39">global_energy_reorder</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::kinetic_attack_intensity" target="global_energy_reorder::oil_price_level" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.75</data>
  <data key="d36">Escalating physical attacks on production, export infrastructure and shipping lanes reduce available crude flows and raise a market risk premium, driving up oil prices.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d39">global_energy_reorder</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::kinetic_attack_intensity" target="us_bond_market_tension::nominal_treasury_yields" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.8</data>
  <data key="d36">A sudden rise in kinetic strikes increases near-term geopolitical risk and safe‑haven demand for U.S. Treasuries, pushing nominal yields down across maturities.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d39">us_bond_market_tension</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::kinetic_attack_intensity" target="us_iran_conflict::vessel_transit_rate" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.55</data>
  <data key="d36">A sudden spike in kinetic attacks that demonstrates expanded targeting or incidental risk to commercial shipping elevates operators' perceived transit risk and prompts some carriers to delay, divert or cancel voyages through the strait, reducing transit counts.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d39">us_iran_conflict</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::kinetic_attack_intensity" target="us_trade_unilateralism::bilateral_trade_volume" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.65</data>
  <data key="d36">Rising kinetic attacks (e.g., in the Black Sea and transport corridors) raise insurance and rerouting costs and prompt export controls or port closures, directly reducing the volume of bilateral goods flows.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d39">us_trade_unilateralism</data>
</edge>
