<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::allied_alignment_level" target="global_energy_reorder::policy_intervention_rate" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.8</data>
  <data key="d36">Higher alignment among allied states produces coordinated market actions (joint purchases, price caps, joint sanctions or strategic stock releases), increasing the frequency and intensity of regulatory and fiscal interventions in energy markets.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d39">global_energy_reorder</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::allied_alignment_level" target="us_bond_market_tension::policy_rate_path" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.55</data>
  <data key="d36">Higher allied alignment tends to produce coordinated fiscal and military spending and sustained policy responses that raise near‑term growth and inflation expectations, leading markets to price a higher future policy‑rate path.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d39">us_bond_market_tension</data>
</edge>
