<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::sanctions_severity" target="global_energy_reorder::lng_gas_flow_volume" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.8</data>
  <data key="d36">Broader sanctions on finance, shipping, insurance and servicing of energy firms directly constrain the ability to load, insure and deliver LNG cargoes from affected suppliers, reducing traded flow volumes.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d39">global_energy_reorder</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::sanctions_severity" target="us_bond_market_tension::portfolio_flows" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.65</data>
  <data key="d36">More severe sanctions disrupt energy/commodity markets and raise counterparty risk, prompting investors to reallocate from equities/EM into perceived safe assets such as U.S. government bonds, increasing net flows into bond assets.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d39">us_bond_market_tension</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::sanctions_severity" target="us_iran_conflict::strait_oil_export_rate" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.7</data>
  <data key="d36">Tighter, more comprehensive sanctions on Russian oil/energy exports reduce available Russian supply on global markets, driving buyers to increase imports from Persian Gulf producers and thereby raising oil volumes passing through the strait.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d39">us_iran_conflict</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::sanctions_severity" target="us_trade_unilateralism::applied_tariff_level" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.8</data>
  <data key="d36">Escalation in sanctions on Russia prompts the US (and aligned partners) to add tariff-based trade restrictions and broaden tariff lines as enforcement and secondary-targeting tools, raising average applied tariff rates on affected imports.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d39">us_trade_unilateralism</data>
</edge>
