<edge source="us_bond_market_tension::policy_rate_path" target="global_energy_reorder::policy_intervention_rate" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.55</data>
  <data key="d36">Market expectations of a prolonged tighter US policy path raise debt‑service and currency pressures for energy‑importing governments, prompting more frequent and intense government interventions (subsidies, price caps, state procurement) to shield domestic consumers and firms.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">us_bond_market_tension</data>
  <data key="d39">global_energy_reorder</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_bond_market_tension::policy_rate_path" target="us_iran_conflict::vessel_transit_rate" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">An upward revision in the expected policy-rate path tightens global financial conditions and raises shipping and commodity-financing costs, reducing demand for oil and other traded goods and thus lowering the number of commercial transits through the strait.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">us_bond_market_tension</data>
  <data key="d39">us_iran_conflict</data>
</edge>
