<edge source="us_trade_unilateralism::corporate_margin_pressur" target="global_energy_reorder::supply_disruption_level" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">Sustained downward pressure on corporate margins in energy firms leads to deferred maintenance and capex cutbacks, increasing the probability and extent of outages and disruptions in energy supply chains.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">us_trade_unilateralism</data>
  <data key="d39">global_energy_reorder</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_trade_unilateralism::corporate_margin_pressur" target="russia_ukraine_war::weapon_transfer_rate" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">Higher tariff-driven input costs and lost sales squeeze defense and defense-adjacent firms' margins, slowing production and deliveries of weapons and thus reducing the pace of transfers into the theatre.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">us_trade_unilateralism</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_trade_unilateralism::corporate_margin_pressur" target="us_bond_market_tension::real_yield_level" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.55</data>
  <data key="d36">Broad increases in corporate margin pressure lower firms' investment and profit growth prospects, reducing aggregate growth expectations and the real term premium investors require, which pushes real yields down.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">us_trade_unilateralism</data>
  <data key="d39">us_bond_market_tension</data>
</edge>
