  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.75</data>
  <data key="d36">Higher oil prices increase inflationary pressure and term premia (through higher expected future deficits and uncertainty), pushing up nominal Treasury yields across maturities.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">global_energy_reorder</data>
  <data key="d39">us_bond_market_tension</data>
