<edge source="global_energy_reorder::supply_disruption_level" target="russia_ukraine_war::kinetic_attack_intensity" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">Acute disruptions to energy and logistics supplies create strategic imperatives to seize or deny critical infrastructure and routes, prompting increased missile, drone and sabotage strikes to secure supplies or impose costs on the adversary.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">global_energy_reorder</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_energy_reorder::supply_disruption_level" target="us_iran_conflict::insurance_premium_level" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.75</data>
  <data key="d36">Visible disruptions to energy supply chains raise perceived loss exposure and volatility for shipments, prompting insurers to raise war‑risk and route‑specific premiums for voyages through the strait.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">global_energy_reorder</data>
  <data key="d39">us_iran_conflict</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_energy_reorder::supply_disruption_level" target="us_trade_unilateralism::bilateral_trade_volume" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.95</data>
  <data key="d36">Physical disruptions to ports, shipping lanes or energy/logistics infrastructure reduce the ability to move goods on schedule or at all, directly lowering the value and quantity of bilateral trade flows.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">global_energy_reorder</data>
  <data key="d39">us_trade_unilateralism</data>
</edge>
