<edge source="global_energy_reorder::policy_intervention_rate" target="russia_ukraine_war::weapon_transfer_rate" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">An uptick in government energy interventions (price caps, subsidies, emergency purchases) frees fiscal space or political capital that governments can reallocate to procurement and transfers of weapons and enabling systems into the theatre.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">global_energy_reorder</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_energy_reorder::policy_intervention_rate" target="us_bond_market_tension::real_yield_level" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">A sustained increase in government energy subsidies and state market interventions financed by higher issuance raises expected sovereign supply and term premia, lifting real yields.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">global_energy_reorder</data>
  <data key="d39">us_bond_market_tension</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_energy_reorder::policy_intervention_rate" target="us_iran_conflict::strait_interference_risk" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.7</data>
  <data key="d36">An uptick in policy measures targeting Iranian energy (sanctions, interdiction authorizations, or forced inspections) creates incentives for retaliatory harassment or escalation by Iran or aligned groups, increasing the risk of interference with transits.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">global_energy_reorder</data>
  <data key="d39">us_iran_conflict</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_energy_reorder::policy_intervention_rate" target="us_trade_unilateralism::applied_tariff_level" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.9</data>
  <data key="d36">A higher frequency/intensity of government market interventions typically includes more frequent use of trade instruments, resulting in a higher applied tariff baseline as authorities deploy tariffs to protect supply chains or domestic producers.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">global_energy_reorder</data>
  <data key="d39">us_trade_unilateralism</data>
</edge>
